course: dictionary
lesson: 3176
title: Emptiness: the space and the feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Emptiness is a noun. It means the state of having nothing, or nobody, inside. «Sound needs something to travel through, air, water or solid things, so in the emptiness of space there is no sound at all.» Here emptiness means a place with nothing in it, so there is no air or water for sound to travel through.
explain: The word can also name a feeling. «A feeling of emptiness» is a sad sense that something is missing in your life, or that nothing matters. Look for clues such as missing, lonely or nothing near the word to find which meaning the writer means.
explain: Feelings of emptiness can be heavy, especially after a loss. If you feel this, it helps to talk to someone you trust, such as a parent, carer or teacher. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Emptiness is a noun, meaning the state of being empty.
fact: «The emptiness of space» means space with nothing in it.
fact: «A feeling of emptiness» means a sad sense that something is missing.
fact: Empty is the root word: an empty box has nothing inside it.
fact: In some religions and philosophies, emptiness can describe a calm state, free from the things that cause worry.
exercise: «Sound needs something to travel through, so in the emptiness of space there is no sound at all.» What does emptiness mean here? | A warm, cosy feeling | A busy city street | A loud noise | *A place with nothing inside
exercise: Mia says, «I feel a big emptiness since my best friend moved away.» What kind of feeling is this? | A hungry tummy | A happy surprise | A burst of excited energy | *A sad feeling that something is missing
exercise: Which word is the root of emptiness? | *empty | emptied | emptier | empties
test:
«The desert had an emptiness that made the travellers feel very small.» What does emptiness suggest here? | *A wide, lonely space with nothing around it | A busy market full of shoppers | A bowl of hot soup | A loud party with music
Which sentence uses emptiness to mean a sad feeling? | *«After the move, she felt an emptiness she could not explain.» | «The room had an emptiness of old toys.» | «The emptiness of the bus was full of laughing children.» | «The jar had a sweet emptiness.»
exam: Ravi says emptiness is just a fancy word for empty. What is the best answer? | Completely wrong, because emptiness means happy | *Partly right: it names the state of having nothing inside, and it can also mean a sad feeling that something is missing | Wrong, because emptiness means a loud sound | Right, it means exactly the same as empty, with no other sense
